Optional bundles without source maps (TRIAGE_NO_SOURCEMAPS; DV-13).

Upstream bundles all 28 desktop entry points at once with linked source maps
(sourcesContent: true) and keeps every output in memory before writing. On
GitHub's 8 GB runners that exhausted memory. Measured on a 16 GB machine
(non-minified desktop bundle, total RSS of the process tree):
- upstream (parallel, source maps): past 7 GB after 93 s (esbuild 6 GB), stopped;
- parallel, no source maps: 6.3 GB peak, 101 s;
- sequential (0002), source maps: esbuild 3.4 GB, then Node ran out of heap;
- sequential, no source maps: 3.7 GB peak, 96 s.
app/build.mjs sets both switches unless --sourcemaps is given. Unset,
nothing changes.

